## Key Learnings
- Many network telemetry features are correlated (redundant); treating them independently increases noise
- BENIGN traffic can exceed “high” thresholds (q99), proving strong context dependency
- Some signals produce poor tradeoffs (high FPR + low TPR), making them operationally unusable alone
- Stable SOC detections require identity/asset baselines and correlation rules, not single metrics

